# Channel B — SEALED (vocabulary · reading · listening · writing · speaking)

Read `docs/CHANNEL_B_SEALED.md` before editing any matched file.

## Mandatory

- **Ask the user for explicit permission** before making any change that could affect Channel B behaviour, UI, APIs, AI prompts, scoring, or layout.
- If the user has not approved Channel B changes in the current task, **stop** and describe what you want to change; wait for approval.
- Channel A fixes must use **isolated** paths (`channel=A`, `source_channel='A'`, admin-only modules). Do not rewrite Channel B branches.

## Do not (without permission)

- Modify `_build_practice_exam_channel_b`, Channel B review/day/calendar logic, or B skill UIs listed in the doc.
- Change shared hub/server/CSS in ways that alter the AI self-study (B) student experience.
- “Clean up” or refactor sealed code if it risks changing B outputs.

## Allowed without unsealing (if truly B-neutral)

- Channel A–only files (e.g. `self_study_vocabulary_ai.py`, `admin-self-study-*.js`) when changes cannot affect B.
- Comments/docs that do not change runtime behaviour.
